WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.894
Fifteen months building

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:02.696
a better coding

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:03.604
agent harness

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:05.336
Mickey Petersen

00:00:05.396 --> 00:00:06.551
author of Mastering

00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:07.046
Emacs

00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:08.674
has released DreamCoder

00:00:08.898 --> 00:00:10.112
a frontier coding

00:00:09.924 --> 00:00:10.643
harness

00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:11.645
with a tiling

00:00:11.457 --> 00:00:12.707
window manager that

00:00:12.518 --> 00:00:13.190
runs in the

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:14.299
browser on all

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.997
three desktop platforms

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.465
He started in

00:00:17.277 --> 00:00:18.574
May 2025

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:20.012
expecting two or

00:00:19.824 --> 00:00:20.708
three months of

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.097
work

00:00:21.236 --> 00:00:22.238
It took fifteen

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.052
months of UI

00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:24.325
and backend iterations

00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:24.844
and a beta

00:00:24.656 --> 00:00:25.281
test

00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:27.382
Petersen argues terminal

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:28.290
coding agents are

00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:29.493
cramped and awkward

00:00:29.305 --> 00:00:30.696
for copying multi-line

00:00:30.507 --> 00:00:31.120
text

00:00:31.227 --> 00:00:32.099
and that most

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:33.431
GUI harnesses look

00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:33.927
the same

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.306
a sidebar and

00:00:35.118 --> 00:00:36.073
a chat pane

00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:37.620
Full story on

00:00:37.431 --> 00:00:38.327
the dashboard
